  "raw_policy_excerpt": "Security is a top priority at inDrive. If you believe you've found a security bug in our in-scope applications or infrastructure, we are happy to work with you to resolve the issue promptly and ensure you are fairly rewarded for your discovery.\n\n#Update to the Scope Policy (from 09/09/2025)\n\ninDrive is not only about ride-hailing - we also contribute to education, sports, environmental initiatives, and other social projects. To make our bug bounty program clearer, we divide the scope into Core and Non-core services:\n- Core services are directly connected to our main app infrastructure (backend, frontend resources). E.g., no-gw-cf.<region>.aws.indriverapp.com, couriers.indrive.com.\n- Non-core services are additional projects of inDrive, such as web resources related to social, non-profit, experimental initiatives and partner integrations.\n\n#We will not pay a reward if we detect:\n* Social engineering directed at the company's employees\n* Attempt to access arbitrary user's account or data or another vulnerability post-exploitation not required to demonstrate the bug presence\n* Distributed network/request flooding and other resource exhaustion attacks. Automated scanning tools must be limited to 5 request per second (300 requests per minute) to one target host summing up all tools and threads running in parallel and must not exceed 5 parallel requests at the same time (5 threads).\n\n#We do not initiate security investigations regarding:\n* Messages from security scanners without clear PoC and impact\n* Self-XSS; Framing; Social engineering; Clickjacking; SPF/DKIM/DMARC issues; Man-in-the-Middle\n* Infrastructure vulnerabilities: Server config issues (open ports, TLS), SSL cert issues, DNS config\n* Google API key (for google maps)\n* Vulnerabilities in partner services not directly affecting inDrive security\n\n#Strictly prohibited: DoS/DDoS attacks; Threats/harm to company employees.\n\n#Reward payment table (Core / Non-core):\n| RCE non-isolated | 15000 / 8000 | Critical |\n| RCE isolated | 8000 / 4000 | High |\n| SQLi | 4000-8000 / 2000-4000 | High-Critical |\n| LFR/RFI/XXE | 4000 / 2000 | High-Critical |\n| SSRF non-blind | 4000 / 1000-2000 | High |\n| SSRF blind | 1500 / 750 | High |\n| Info disclosure critical data | 5000 / 2500 | High |\n| Info disclosure sensitive (bulk) | 2000 / 1000 | High |\n| Info disclosure sensitive (other) | 1000 / 500 | High |\n| Info disclosure low sensitivity | 500 / 250 | Medium |\n| Admin auth bypass | 3000 / 1000-1500 | High |\n| Admin blind XSS | 2000 / 500-1000 | Medium-High |\n| Account takeover (no interaction) | 2000 / 500-800 | Medium-High |\n| Account takeover (with interaction) | 1000 / 400 | Medium-High |\n| Auth bypass (JWT/passkey/OTP/OAuth) | 1000 / 500 | High |\n| XSS | 300-400 / 150-200 | Medium |\n| Subdomain takeover | 100 / 50 | Low |"
